# Shell scripts must check out with LF on every platform.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows, where the common `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites the
# working tree to CRLF on checkout. Git Bash tolerates a stray \r in most lines, so the
# damage is intermittent rather than obvious — but a heredoc delimiter, a `set -e` guard
# or a trailing-backslash continuation with \r attached fails in ways that read as a logic
# bug, not a line-ending bug. The blobs in this repo are already LF; this keeps the
# checkout that way regardless of the user's global setting.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The asset pipeline's PNGs, audio and fonts are binary — never touch them.
*.png binary
*.wav binary
*.ogg binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.aseprite binary

# ADR-013: a compiled shader is binary; its .fx source checks out LF so its recorded SHA-256 matches everywhere.
*.mgfxo binary
*.fx text eol=lf
